sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To an apotome only one rational straight line can be annexed which is commensurable with the whole in square only.
----
proof:

Let {AB} be an apotome, and {BC} an annex to it. Then {AC} and {CB} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only. [!just X.73]

I say that no other rational straight line can be annexed to {AB} which is commensurable with the whole in square only.

